insert into nodes (node_type, slug, title, summary, status, meta_title, meta_description, legacy_slugs, published_at) values ('article', 'beautiful-places-to-visit-in-maldives', 'Beautiful Places to Visit in Maldives', 'Discover the most beautiful places to visit in Maldives, from pristine beaches to vibrant coral reefs. Explore top resorts, islands, and atolls that make the Maldives a tropical paradise.', 'published', 'Beautiful Places to Visit in Maldives | Maldives Travel Guide | MTG', 'Discover the most beautiful places to visit in Maldives, from pristine beaches to vibrant coral reefs. Explore top resorts, islands, and atolls that make the Maldives a tropical paradise.', ARRAY['/articles/beautiful-places-to-visit-in-Maldives.html']::text[], now()) on conflict (node_type, slug) do nothing;
insert into articles (id, body, reading_time_minutes) select id, '<p>The Maldives, a paradise on earth, is a dream destination for travelers from around the globe. This tropical archipelago, composed of 26 atolls and over 1,000 coral islands, offers an unparalleled experience with its turquoise waters, white sandy beaches, and vibrant marine life. Whether you''re planning a family vacation, a romantic getaway, or an adventure-filled trip, the Maldives has something for everyone. In this article, we''ll explore some of the most beautiful places to visit in the Maldives, along with recommendations for families, couples, and those looking to explore the capital city of Male.</p><h3>Quick Navigations (Topics covered in this guide)</h3><p>Places to Visit in Maldives for Couples Places to Visit in Maldives for Family Places to Visit in Male</p><h2>1. Places to Visit in Maldives for Couples</h2><h3>1.1 Veligandu Island</h3><p>Veligandu Island is renowned for its romantic ambiance, making it a top destination for couples. With its overwater bungalows, private beaches, and stunning sunsets, it''s perfect for honeymooners and those looking to rekindle romance. Couples can enjoy spa treatments, candlelit dinners on the beach, and explore the surrounding coral reefs.</p><h4>Water Villas and Private Pools:</h4><p>Veligandu Island is renowned for its luxurious water villas, many of which feature private pools overlooking the crystal-clear lagoon. These villas offer the ultimate in privacy, allowing couples to enjoy each other''s company in a serene environment. Imagine waking up to the gentle sounds of the ocean, enjoying breakfast on your private deck, and taking a dip in the warm waters directly from your villa.</p><h3>1.2 Baros Maldives</h3><p>Baros Maldives is a luxurious resort that offers privacy and elegance, ideal for a romantic getaway. The resort features secluded villas, some with private pools, and exceptional dining experiences. Activities such as sunset cruises, diving, and couples'' massages add to the romantic atmosphere.</p><h4>Baros Lighthouse Restaurant:</h4><p>For couples who are food enthusiasts, dining at the Baros Lighthouse Restaurant is a must. This overwater restaurant offers panoramic views of the ocean and serves exquisite gourmet meals prepared by world-class chefs. The romantic setting is enhanced by the sound of the waves and the gentle sea breeze, making it an unforgettable dining experience.</p><h4>Diving and Snorkeling:</h4><p>Baros is also a great destination for couples who enjoy exploring the underwater world. The island is home to some of the best diving and snorkeling spots in the Maldives, with vibrant coral reefs and an abundance of marine life. Whether you''re a seasoned diver or a beginner, Baros offers personalized diving experiences that can be enjoyed together.</p><figure><img src="legacy/resorts/baros-island/images/baros-maldives-island-resort.webp" alt="Baros Maldives" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>1.3 Cocoa Island by COMO</h3><p>Known for its unique dhoni boat-inspired villas, Cocoa Island offers couples an intimate setting to relax and rejuvenate. The resort provides private yoga sessions, snorkeling adventures, and beachside dining, all set against the backdrop of the pristine Maldivian waters.</p><h4>Spa and Wellness:</h4><p>The COMO Shambhala Retreat on Cocoa Island is renowned for its holistic wellness treatments, making it a perfect destination for couples looking to relax and rejuvenate. From couples'' massages to yoga sessions overlooking the ocean, the retreat offers a range of experiences designed to nurture both body and soul.</p><h4>Private Excursions:</h4><p>Cocoa Island offers a variety of private excursions, such as sunset fishing trips, dolphin watching, and visits to nearby uninhabited islands. These personalized experiences allow you to explore the beauty of the Maldives together, creating memories that will last a lifetime.</p><h3>1.4 Mirihi Island</h3><p>Mirihi Island is a small, exclusive resort known for its tranquility and stunning natural beauty. With just a few villas, it ensures privacy and personalized service. Couples can enjoy diving, sailing, and exploring the vibrant house reef.</p><h4>Private Yacht Charters:</h4><p>Couples can charter a private yacht for a day of sailing, snorkeling, and island hopping. The yacht comes fully equipped with luxury amenities, and the crew can arrange a special lunch or dinner on a secluded island, ensuring a memorable day at sea.</p><h4>Mirihi Moments:</h4><p>The resort offers &quot;Mirihi Moments,&quot; personalized experiences designed to create unforgettable memories. This can include a private beach dinner, a sunset dolphin cruise, or a day trip to a deserted island. Each moment is crafted to offer a unique and intimate experience for couples.</p><h3>1.5 Soneva Fushi</h3><p>Soneva Fushi is a luxurious resort that offers a blend of barefoot luxury and natural beauty. Couples can indulge in the Robinson Crusoe experience, with private villas nestled in the lush jungle or over the water.</p><h4>Private Cinema Paradiso:</h4><p>One of the standout features of Soneva Fushi is its outdoor cinema, Cinema Paradiso. Imagine watching a classic movie under the stars while lounging on a plush daybed, with the sound of the ocean in the background. This private cinema experience can be customized with your choice of movie, snacks, and drinks, making it a perfect date night activity.</p><h4>Eco-Friendly Villas:</h4><p>Soneva Fushi is known for its eco-friendly approach to luxury, with villas that blend seamlessly into the natural environment. Each villa is surrounded by lush greenery and offers direct access to the beach, providing a private and tranquil retreat. The villas are designed with sustainability in mind, featuring solar panels, natural ventilation, and organic materials, allowing you to enjoy a luxurious stay while minimizing your environmental impact.</p><figure><img src="legacy/resorts/soneva-fushi/images/soneva-fushi-island-resort-maldives.webp" alt="Soneva Fushi" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>1.6 Huvafen Fushi</h3><p>Huvafen Fushi is home to the world''s first underwater spa, making it a truly unique destination for couples. The resort offers a blend of contemporary design and natural beauty, creating a luxurious and romantic atmosphere.</p><h4>Private Lagoon Dinners:</h4><p>For an extraordinary dining experience, Huvafen Fushi offers private lagoon dinners. A table is set up in the shallow waters of the lagoon, where you can enjoy a gourmet meal with your feet in the sand and the water gently lapping around you. The setting sun and the sounds of the ocean create a magical atmosphere that''s perfect for a special occasion.</p><h4>Luxury Beach and Ocean Villas:</h4><p>Huvafen Fushi offers a range of luxurious villas, each with its own private plunge pool and direct access to the beach or the lagoon. The spacious villas are designed with romance in mind, featuring outdoor showers, sun decks, and even outdoor baths for a truly indulgent experience.</p><h3>1.7 The St. Regis Maldives Vommuli Resort</h3><p>The St. Regis Maldives Vommuli Resort offers unparalleled luxury, with stunning architecture, world-class amenities, and exceptional service. It''s a top choice for couples looking to indulge in the finer things in life.</p><h4>Experiences for Couples:</h4><p>The resort offers a range of activities for couples, including sunset cruises, private yacht charters, and personalized excursions. The overwater villas feature private pools, outdoor showers, and direct access to the lagoon.</p><h4>Spa and Wellness:</h4><p>The Iridium Spa at St. Regis offers a luxurious sanctuary for couples, with overwater treatment rooms, a hydrotherapy pool, and a relaxation lounge. The spa''s signature treatments are designed to rejuvenate and refresh.</p><h3>1.8 Six Senses Laamu</h3><p>Six Senses Laamu combines luxury with sustainability, offering couples a romantic retreat that''s also eco-friendly. The resort''s commitment to preserving the natural environment adds a sense of purpose to your stay.</p><h4>Dining Under the Stars:</h4><p>The resort offers several dining options, but one of the most romantic is a private dinner on the beach, under the stars. You can enjoy a personalized menu created by the resort''s chefs, with your table set up on the soft sand and surrounded by lanterns. The sound of the waves and the starlit sky provide the perfect ambiance for an unforgettable evening with your loved one.</p><h4>Overwater Villas with Glass Floors:</h4><p>The overwater villas at Six Senses Laamu are designed to bring the beauty of the ocean into your living space. Each villa features a glass floor panel, allowing you to watch the marine life swimming below. The villas also come with private decks, outdoor showers, and direct access to the lagoon, offering a luxurious and romantic setting for your stay.</p><figure><img src="legacy/resorts/six-senses-laamu/images/six-senses-laamu-maldives.webp" alt="Six Senses Laamu" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>1.9 Conrad Maldives Rangali Island</h3><p>Conrad Maldives Rangali Island offers one of the most unique dining experiences in the world at Ithaa, an underwater restaurant. Couples can enjoy a gourmet meal surrounded by the vibrant marine life of the Maldives, creating an unforgettable romantic experience.</p><h4>Private Movie Night on the Beach:</h4><p>Conrad Maldives offers a private beach cinema experience where couples can watch a movie under the stars. The resort sets up a large screen on the beach, complete with cozy loungers, blankets, and snacks, creating a magical setting for a romantic evening.</p><h4>Wine and Cheese Sunset Cruise:</h4><p>Couples can embark on a sunset cruise aboard a traditional Maldivian dhoni, enjoying a selection of fine wines and cheeses while watching the sun set over the horizon. The cruise offers stunning views and a relaxing atmosphere, perfect for winding down after a day of exploring.</p><h3>1.10 Rangali Island</h3><p>Rangali Island is home to the world-famous Ithaa Undersea Restaurant, an all-glass restaurant located 16 feet below the surface of the ocean. Dining at Ithaa is a once-in-a-lifetime experience, where you can enjoy a gourmet meal surrounded by panoramic views of the coral reef and marine life. The restaurant''s unique setting makes it an ideal choice for a romantic dinner or even a proposal.</p><h4>Romantic Sailing:</h4><p>Rangali Island also offers a range of romantic sailing experiences, from private yacht charters to traditional dhoni sunset cruises. Sailing through the turquoise waters of the Maldives, with the wind in your hair and your loved one by your side, is an unforgettable way to experience the beauty of this tropical paradise.</p><h4>Spa Treatments for Two:</h4><p>The resort''s spa offers a variety of treatments designed for couples, including massages, facials, and body wraps. The spa''s treatment rooms overlook the ocean, providing a peaceful and serene environment where you can relax and unwind together.</p><h3>1.11 Lily Beach Resort &amp; Spa</h3><p>Lily Beach Resort &amp; Spa is perfect for couples seeking a mix of luxury and adventure. The resort offers &quot;Romantic Escapes&quot; packages that include a variety of couple-centric activities such as private dining experiences, sunset cruises, and rejuvenating spa treatments. The lush surroundings and crystal-clear waters provide the ideal backdrop for a romantic getaway.</p><h4>Overwater Villas:</h4><p>The overwater villas at Lily Beach offer an unparalleled experience of luxury and privacy. Each villa features a private deck with direct access to the lagoon, allowing couples to swim, snorkel, or simply relax while enjoying the panoramic views of the Indian Ocean.</p><h4>Tamarind Restaurant:</h4><p>For a unique dining experience, Tamarind Restaurant offers a fusion of Thai and Indian cuisine in an intimate setting. The restaurant''s overwater location and carefully crafted menu make it an ideal spot for a romantic dinner.</p><figure><img src="legacy/resorts/lily-beach/images/lily-beach-resort-and-spa-maldives-island.webp" alt="Lily Beach Resort &amp; Spa" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>1.12 Anantara Veli Maldives Resort</h3><p>Anantara Veli Maldives Resort is a favorite among couples for its luxurious overwater spa. The spa offers a variety of treatments that can be enjoyed individually or as a couple, with the option to book a private treatment room with stunning ocean views.</p><h4>Gulhifushi Island Picnic:</h4><p>The resort offers a unique experience with a picnic on Gulhifushi Island, a private island accessible only to resort guests. Couples can spend the day exploring the island, snorkeling, and enjoying a gourmet picnic on the beach, with no one else around.</p><h4>Aqua Retreat:</h4><p>For the ultimate in luxury and privacy, the Aqua Retreat at Anantara Veli offers a secluded two-bedroom villa with a private infinity pool, outdoor showers, and direct access to the lagoon. The retreat is perfect for couples looking to escape and enjoy a romantic and relaxing stay in paradise.</p><h2>2. Places to Visit in Maldives for Family</h2><h3>2.1 Kurumba Maldives</h3><h4>Family-Friendly Resort:</h4><p>Kurumba Maldives is one of the most family-friendly resorts in the Maldives. It offers a range of activities for children and adults, including kids'' clubs, snorkeling, and cultural performances. The resort''s proximity to Male makes it convenient for families looking to explore the capital as well.</p><h4>Activities for All Ages:</h4><p>Kurumba offers a variety of activities that appeal to all age groups, from snorkeling and water sports to cultural tours and cooking classes. The resort''s marine biology program is particularly popular with children, offering interactive learning experiences about the local marine life.</p><h4>Kids'' Club:</h4><p>The kids'' club at Kurumba offers a range of supervised activities, including arts and crafts, treasure hunts, and themed days. This allows parents to enjoy some time alone while their children are entertained in a safe and fun environment.</p><figure><img src="legacy/resorts/kurumba/images/kurumba-maldives-vihamanaafushi-resort.webp" alt="Kurumba Maldives" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>2.2 Sun Island Resort &amp; Spa</h3><p>Sun Island Resort &amp; Spa offers spacious family suites that provide plenty of room for everyone to relax. The resort is known for its wide range of activities that cater to both adults and children, making it an excellent choice for family vacations.</p><h4>Adventure Activities:</h4><p>Families can enjoy a variety of adventure activities, including windsurfing, canoeing, and diving. The resort also offers guided nature walks and excursions to nearby islands, providing educational experiences for children.</p><h4>Eco-Friendly Experiences:</h4><p>The resort emphasizes sustainability and offers eco-friendly experiences such as coral planting and marine conservation tours. These activities are both educational and fun, helping children learn about the importance of protecting the environment.</p><h3>2.3 Dhigurah Island</h3><p>For families looking to experience the local culture, Dhigurah Island is an excellent choice. This inhabited island offers a more authentic experience of Maldivian life, with opportunities to interact with locals, explore the island, and enjoy traditional Maldivian cuisine.</p><h4>Family-Friendly Beaches:</h4><p>Dhigurah Island boasts long stretches of family-friendly beaches where children can safely play in the shallow waters. The island''s calm and serene environment makes it an ideal spot for families to relax and enjoy the natural beauty of the Maldives.</p><h4>Whale Shark Snorkeling:</h4><p>Dhigurah is located near some of the best whale shark snorkeling spots in the Maldives. Families can embark on guided snorkeling tours to see these gentle giants up close, creating a thrilling and educational experience for children.</p><h3>2.4 Bandos Maldives</h3><p>Bandos Maldives is conveniently located near Male, making it an excellent choice for families who want easy access to the capital city. The resort is also close to the international airport, reducing travel time and making it a convenient option for families with young children.</p><h4>Kids'' Club and Babysitting Services:</h4><p>Bandos Maldives offers a well-equipped kids'' club with a variety of activities, including arts and crafts, games, and outdoor play. The resort also provides babysitting services, allowing parents to enjoy some time alone while their children are entertained.</p><h4>Family Dining Options:</h4><p>The resort features several family-friendly dining options, with menus that cater to both adults and children. Special themed nights and buffets ensure that everyone in the family can find something they enjoy.</p><h3>2.5 Reethi Faru Resort</h3><p>Reethi Faru Resort is an eco-friendly resort that is ideal for families interested in sustainable travel. The resort''s focus on environmental conservation and education provides a great learning opportunity for children and adults alike.</p><h4>Diving and Snorkeling:</h4><p>The house reef at Reethi Faru is perfect for family snorkeling adventures, offering a chance to see a wide variety of marine life. The resort also offers diving courses for beginners, allowing families to explore the underwater world together.</p><h4>Cultural and Environmental Education:</h4><p>Reethi Faru offers educational programs that focus on Maldivian culture and environmental conservation. These programs include guided tours of the island, cultural workshops, and presentations by marine biologists, providing a rich and informative experience for families.</p><h3>2.6 Meeru Island Resort &amp; Spa</h3><p>Meeru Island Resort &amp; Spa is an all-inclusive family-friendly resort that offers a wide range of activities and amenities catering to families. The resort''s spacious villas and family suites provide comfortable accommodation options, with some offering direct beach access.</p><h4>Family Activities:</h4><p>The resort offers a plethora of activities suitable for all ages, including a kids'' club, sports facilities, and family-friendly excursions. Families can enjoy activities such as snorkeling, diving, and island hopping, making it a perfect choice for an adventurous family holiday.</p><h4>Entertainment and Dining:</h4><p>Meeru Island Resort &amp; Spa provides entertainment for the whole family with live music, cultural performances, and themed nights. The resort also features several restaurants with kid-friendly menus, ensuring that even the pickiest eaters are well-catered to.</p><h3>2.7 Kuredu Island Resort &amp; Spa</h3><p>Kuredu Island Resort &amp; Spa is a large resort with extensive amenities that cater to families. The resort offers family villas with private pools, multiple dining options, and a variety of activities that appeal to all age groups.</p><h4>Kid''s Club and Teen Programs:</h4><p>The resort''s kids'' club offers a wide range of activities for younger children, including arts and crafts, games, and educational programs. For teenagers, Kuredu offers sports facilities, a dive center, and adventure activities like windsurfing and wakeboarding.</p><h4>Family Excursions:</h4><p>Kuredu Island Resort &amp; Spa offers a variety of family-friendly excursions, including dolphin safaris, snorkeling trips, and sunset cruises. These excursions provide the perfect opportunity for families to explore the natural beauty of the Maldives together.</p><h3>2.8 Hideaway Beach Resort &amp; Spa</h3><p>Hideaway Beach Resort &amp; Spa offers a private and secluded environment that is perfect for families looking for a peaceful getaway. The resort''s large villas and residences provide ample space for families, with some offering private pools and direct beach access.</p><h4>Kids'' and Teens'' Club:</h4><p>The resort features both a kids'' club and a teens'' club, offering a variety of activities designed to engage and entertain children of all ages. Activities include treasure hunts, movie nights, and water sports, ensuring that children and teenagers have plenty of options to keep them busy.</p><h4>Family Dining and Experiences:</h4><p>Hideaway Beach Resort &amp; Spa offers family-friendly dining options with menus that cater to both adults and children. The resort also provides unique family experiences, such as private beach dinners, movie nights under the stars, and family yoga sessions.</p><figure><img src="legacy/resorts/hideaway-beach/images/hideaway-beach-island-resort-and-spa.webp" alt="Hideaway Beach Resort &amp; Spa in Maldives" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>2.9 Vakkaru Maldives</h3><p>Vakkaru Maldives is a luxurious and elegant retreat that caters to families with its spacious beach and overwater villas. The resort''s tranquil environment and world-class amenities provide a serene setting for a family vacation.</p><h4>Marine Biology Programs:</h4><p>Vakkaru Maldives offers a variety of marine biology programs that are both fun and educational for children and adults. These programs include guided snorkeling tours, coral planting activities, and marine biology talks, providing an in-depth understanding of the local marine ecosystem.</p><h4>Family Adventures:</h4><p>Families can participate in a range of adventures, including dolphin cruises, fishing trips, and island excursions. The resort also offers family yoga sessions, tennis lessons, and other activities that allow families to bond and create lasting memories.</p><h3>2.10 The Sun Siyam Iru Fushi</h3><p>The Sun Siyam Iru Fushi is a family-friendly island resort that offers a variety of accommodation options, including beach villas and overwater villas, suitable for families of all sizes. The resort''s extensive facilities and activities make it an ideal choice for a family vacation.</p><h4>Kids'' Club and Family Activities:</h4><p>The resort''s kids'' club offers a range of activities, including arts and crafts, nature walks, and cooking classes. For families, the resort offers excursions such as dolphin cruises, snorkeling trips, and cultural experiences that provide entertainment and education.</p><h4>Wellness and Relaxation:</h4><p>The Sun Siyam Iru Fushi offers family-friendly wellness activities, including yoga sessions, family spa treatments, and meditation classes. The resort''s spa also offers treatments specifically designed for younger guests, making it a great place for families to relax together.</p><h2>3. Places to Visit in Male</h2><h3>3.1 Male Friday Mosque (Hukuru Miskiy)</h3><h4>Historical Significance:</h4><p>Male Friday Mosque, also known as Hukuru Miskiy, is one of the oldest and most significant mosques in the Maldives. Built in 1658, this mosque is renowned for its intricate coral stone architecture, traditional wood carvings, and beautiful lacquer work. It is a UNESCO World Heritage site and a must-visit for history enthusiasts.</p><h4>Cultural Experience:</h4><p>Visitors to Hukuru Miskiy can explore the history and cultural heritage of the Maldives through the mosque''s ancient inscriptions, tombstones, and architectural features. The mosque is still active, so it''s important to dress modestly and respect the local customs while visiting.</p><h3>3.2 The National Museum</h3><h4>Cultural and Historical Insights:</h4><p>The National Museum of Maldives is located in Sultan Park, housed in a former royal palace. The museum showcases the rich history and culture of the Maldives, with exhibits ranging from ancient artifacts and royal regalia to traditional costumes and weapons.</p><h4>Educational Experience:</h4><p>Visitors can learn about the Maldives'' history, from its Buddhist period to the Islamic era, through the museum''s extensive collection. It''s an excellent place for families and history buffs to gain deeper insights into the Maldives'' past.</p><h3>3.3 The President''s Palace (Mulee Aage)</h3><h4>Architectural Marvel:</h4><p>Mulee Aage, the official residence of the President of the Maldives, is a striking example of colonial architecture in Male. Built in the early 20th century, the palace is known for its elaborate carvings, vibrant colors, and well-manicured gardens.</p><h4>Photography Spot:</h4><p>While visitors are not allowed inside the palace, the exterior offers a great opportunity for photography. The palace''s distinctive style makes it a popular stop on walking tours of Male.</p><h3>3.4 Sultan Park and Rasrani Bageecha</h3><h4>Urban Oasis:</h4><p>Sultan Park, also known as Rasrani Bageecha, is a lush green space in the heart of Male, offering a peaceful retreat from the city''s hustle and bustle. The park was once part of the royal palace grounds and now features well-maintained gardens, playgrounds, and water features.</p><h4>Family-Friendly Attraction:</h4><p>Sultan Park is an ideal spot for families to relax, with plenty of shaded areas, benches, and play areas for children. The park is also home to the National Museum, making it a convenient stop for those exploring Male''s cultural sites.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/male/sultan-park-male.webp" alt="Sultan Park and Rasrani Bageecha" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>3.5 Maldives Islamic Centre</h3><h4>Iconic Landmark:</h4><p>The Maldives Islamic Centre is one of the most prominent landmarks in Male. The center is known for its large golden dome, which dominates the city''s skyline. The mosque inside the Islamic Centre is the largest in the Maldives and can accommodate over 5,000 worshippers.</p><h4>Cultural Understanding:</h4><p>Visitors are welcome to explore the mosque outside of prayer times, providing an opportunity to learn about Islamic architecture and culture in the Maldives. The Islamic Centre also hosts various cultural events and exhibitions throughout the year.</p><h3>3.6 Artificial Beach</h3><h4>Recreational Spot:</h4><p>Artificial Beach is a man-made beach located on the eastern side of Male. It''s a popular spot for locals and tourists alike, offering a place to swim, relax, and enjoy the sunset. The beach is also a hub for various water sports and beach activities.</p><h4>Community Events:</h4><p>Artificial Beach often hosts community events, including music festivals, parades, and carnivals. It''s a great place to experience the local culture and enjoy some leisure time by the sea.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/male/male-city-artificial-beach.webp" alt="Artificial Beach" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>3.7 Victory Monument</h3><h4>Historical Monument:</h4><p>The Victory Monument in Male commemorates the victory of the Maldives government over a coup attempt in 1988. The monument is located near the Republic Square and serves as a reminder of the country''s political history.</p><h4>Quick Visit:</h4><p>While not a major tourist attraction, the Victory Monument is worth a quick visit for those interested in the Maldives'' modern history. It''s located in a central area, making it easy to include in a walking tour of Male.</p><h3>3.8 Hulhumale Island</h3><h4>Modern Development:</h4><p>Hulhumale is a reclaimed island located just a short ferry ride from Male. The island was developed to address the population growth in Male and features modern infrastructure, residential areas, and beautiful beaches.</p><h4>Day Trip Destination:</h4><p>Hulhumale offers a variety of activities for visitors, including beach outings, water sports, and dining at seaside restaurants. It''s a great day trip destination for families and those looking to escape the hustle of Male.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/hulhumale-city-maldives.webp" alt="Hulhumale Island" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>3.9 Tsunami Monument</h3><h4>Urban Oasis:</h4><p>The Tsunami Monument, located on the southeastern part of Male, commemorates the lives lost in the 2004 Indian Ocean tsunami. The monument features a unique design with spheres representing the victims and steel rods symbolizing the impact of the waves.</p><h4>Reflective Spot:</h4><p>Visitors to the Tsunami Monument can reflect on the tragedy and resilience of the Maldivian people. The surrounding area offers a peaceful environment with views of the ocean.</p><h3>3.10 Villingili Island</h3><h4>Quiet Getaway:</h4><p>Villingili Island, also known as Villimale, is a quiet residential island located just west of Male. The island is accessible by a short ferry ride and offers a more relaxed atmosphere compared to the bustling capital.</p><h4>Local Experience:</h4><p>Villingili is a great place to experience local life, with its quiet streets, small cafes, and local shops. The island''s beaches are less crowded, making it a perfect spot for a peaceful day trip.</p><h3>3.11 Fish Market</h3><h4>Local Culture:</h4><p>The Fish Market in Male is a vibrant and bustling place where locals buy and sell fresh seafood. It''s an excellent spot to witness the daily life of Male''s residents and experience the local food culture.</p><h4>Culinary Adventure:</h4><p>Visitors can observe the fishermen as they bring in their catch of the day and even purchase fresh fish to be cooked at nearby restaurants. The market is a lively spot that offers a glimpse into the traditional Maldivian way of life.</p><h3>3.12 Republic Square</h3><h4>Central Hub:</h4><p>Republic Square, also known as Jumhooree Maidhaan, is a central square in Male that serves as a popular gathering place for locals. The square is surrounded by important government buildings, including the Presidential Palace and the headquarters of the Maldivian National Defence Force.</p><h4>Local Events:</h4><p>Republic Square is often the site of national celebrations, parades, and other public events. It''s a great place to visit to observe the local culture and enjoy the city''s vibrant atmosphere.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/male/male-city-republic-square.webp" alt="Republic Square" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>3.13 Sinamale Bridge</h3><h4>Engineering Feat:</h4><p>The Sinamale Bridge, also known as the China-Maldives Friendship Bridge, connects Male with Hulhule Island, where Velana International Airport is located. The bridge is a significant engineering achievement and has improved transportation between the islands.</p><h4>Scenic Views:</h4><p>Visitors can take a walk or drive across the bridge to enjoy panoramic views of the Indian Ocean and the surrounding islands. The bridge is particularly beautiful at sunset, making it a great spot for photography.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/male/male-bridge.webp" alt="Sinamale Bridge" loading="lazy" /></figure><h3>3.14 Rasfannu Beach</h3><h4>Urban Beach:</h4><p>Rasfannu Beach is a small but popular urban beach located on the western side of Male. The beach offers a convenient spot for swimming, sunbathing, and relaxing, with facilities such as showers, changing rooms, and food stalls nearby.</p><h4>Sunset Views:</h4><p>Rasfannu Beach is a great place to catch the sunset in Male. The beach is well-maintained and offers a laid-back atmosphere, making it a favorite spot for both locals and tourists.</p><figure><img src="legacy/images/male/male-city-beach.webp" alt="Rasfannu Beach" loading="lazy" /></figure>', 22 from nodes where node_type = 'article' and slug = 'beautiful-places-to-visit-in-maldives' on conflict (id) do nothing;
